From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 15:16:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 71/76] docs(witness): document the no-such-bead reap route and
 its two new events (gcp-ac59)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The reap fix in 0307891 added a second removal authority to
polecat-worktree-reap.sh and two log events with it, but the witness-facing
documentation still described only the closed-bead path. That gap matters more
here than it usually would: the reaper log is the witness's ONLY signal for this
class of stranded work, so an event the runbook does not explain is an event the
patrol cannot act on. `worktree_unpublished_kept` in particular is a real
finding that never resolves itself — left undocumented it reads like the routine
skips around it and gets ignored every cycle.

mol-witness-patrol's reap-merged-worktrees step now describes both routes: why a
leaf that is not a bead id can never satisfy gates 2 and 4, why the
transient/permanent split keys on bd's own error class rather than a guess at id
shape, and gate 5 (HEAD reachable from a remote-tracking ref) as the evidence
that substitutes for bead closure on that path alone. The pre-existing paragraph
explaining why the CLOSED-bead path is deliberately not gated on publication is
kept and re-scoped to "that path", so gate 5 does not read as a reversal of it.
The lead-in that promised "all four gates" is reworded, since the list it
introduces now runs to five and the fifth belongs to the other authority.

The event table gains rows for `worktree_no_such_bead` and
`worktree_unpublished_kept`, and the existing `worktree_bead_unreadable` row is
tightened — its meaning narrowed when the permanent case split out of it, so the
row now says it covers a fuzzy hit or a per-id read failure and stays transient,
and points at the new row for an id bd positively reports as absent. The witness
prompt template gets the same two facts in miniature, matching the summary depth
already there rather than duplicating the step.

Also corrects a stub comment in the test file to name `gc bd show`, the
invocation the stub actually intercepts.

Validation: full gastown shell suite (11/11) and the Python suite (116 passed,
7 skipped) green, including test_prompt_formula_command_drift.py and
test_no_bare_bd_commands.py, which are the two that police exactly this kind of
prose-and-formula edit. Documentation only — no behavior change.
