-**What it will and will not remove.** All four gates must hold:
+**What it will and will not remove.** There are two removal authorities.
+On the ordinary one — a worktree under a bead — all four of these must
+hold:
 
 1. The path is a per-bead polecat worktree
    (`.../polecats/<agent>/worktrees/<bead-id>`). A polecat's persistent
@@ -581,11 +583,27 @@ in it. Treat the log as a report, not as a completed cleanup.
    fails is not proof of absence, the same rule the orphan-recovery step
